From dde844a78ffb63c8a9429466ac2830b6deb62ba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:22:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Wind and a painted sky under the new look: swaying trees and
 grass, drifting clouds

The world never stands still now, as WoW Forever's doesn't. One wind
blows for the whole world, the same for every hero: a fixed function of
the server's clock (a steady prevailing push and three slowly turning
parts, so it drifts over hours), a breeze rolled per server day, calmer
at night, wilder in a storm, with soft gust fronts crossing the ground
downwind so neighbouring trees bend one after another. In the vertex
stage the trees and bushes (doodads whose model names a plant) lean and
sway with height above their base, each on its own phase, the trunk
still and the leaves fluttering a little; the ground clutter bends from
its roots in a ripple running downwind; the shadow pass sways them too.
Models that sway by their own bones are skinned and left alone.

The sky is painted: one layer over 1.12's dome, discs and stars, in its
cloud dome's slot. Soft domain-warped clouds drift in the same wind,
thin on a clear day and thicker as the day, the zone or a storm says,
lit by the hour (pink at dawn, white at noon, gold underneath at golden
hour, blue-grey at night) in soft painted bands with silver edges toward
the sun, going into the haze at the horizon. The sun gets a warm halo
on the god rays' own sun, the moon a pale one; the clouds cover the
stars and the discs, and the cloud over the sun dims its glare, its
rays and the water's glint. The water's mirror runs the same clouds, so
the lakes reflect them.

worldWind 0 and worldSky 0 turn each off on its own; lookwind
<strength 0-3> [gust 0-3] | grade and looksky clouds <0-1> | grade hold
them for film; worldLook 0 is 1.12 untouched.

